      "raw_mention": "$Z",
      "text": "@taleino93 @nejatian Hmm, looked into it more. While the Allosaurus pattern is promising, for $HPP, triple rate cut doesn't really affect leasing too much compared to home sales like $Z or $OPEN. It usually encourages hiring but we got the H1-B drama, which isn't helpful either.\n\nThey have a lot of debt, 85.4% of the debt is fixed so it doesn't really benefit from rate cuts like companies that use floating interest do on top. \n\nIt is below NAV though, usually there's another reason why it's below NAV that other hedge funds priced in. I don't know enough to say whether one party is wrong or not. \n\nI'm not too bullish, but maybe the dinosaur sees something I don't.",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/1970267588988219546",
      "kind": "reply",
